                <pb facs="0803" n="709" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg709"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lee to Mr. Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-10-17"><hi rendition="#italic">October 17,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With further reference to my dispatch No.
                    160, of the 3d instant, and instruction No. 119, of 8th instant, relative to the
                    case of Charles Govin, I have the honor to transmit copy translation of a
                    communication from the Governor-General, in which he states the name of the
                    officer who reported Govin’s death to have been Brig. Gen. Eduardo Lopez Ochoa,
                    and the place where said official report was written was Jaruco.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fitzhugh Lee.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d639-a1.xml" xpointer="d639-a1"/>
